<model>
    <mount>//OPNsense/XGS</mount>
    <version>1.0.0</version>
    <description>XGS coprocessor</description>
    <items>
        <!--
            One field, and it is deliberately one.

            Everything else the coprocessor can be told is reachable only through the rpc sysctls,
            which are instruments: they stage a request, they have no idea what the firewall is
            doing, and a wrong value in one of them is a dropped LAN rather than a rejected form.
            They do not belong behind a save button. This container holds the one setting that is
            a setting - a switch the appliance's owner is entitled to decide - and bringup.sh
            reads it back out of config.xml by exactly this path, so the names here are not free.
        -->
        <general>
            <offload type="BooleanField">
                <Required>Y</Required>
                <!--
                    Off.

                    Three reasons, in the order they were learned. The coprocessor comes up with
                    fw_cfg 0x2 - TCP_SEQ_CHK alone, no offload - so off is also what the hardware
                    itself defaults to, and a plugin that silently differed from the hardware
                    would be the first thing to suspect and the last thing anybody looked at.

                    Then: with the gate open, a frame that the fast path decides it can handle
                    does not reach pf. That is the entire point of it, and it is also the reason
                    it is not a default. Nothing in this package may quietly take traffic out of
                    the firewall's path on the strength of having been installed.

                    And: as of this version, opening the gate accelerates nothing. Every frame
                    still reaches the host, because no flow is ever activated - see
                    docs/the-state-is-the-gate.md. So the honest default is the one that changes
                    nothing until there is something to change.
                -->
                <Default>0</Default>
            </offload>
        </general>
    </items>
</model>
